  "conclusion": "Condition B (discrete units, LVE=8.08e-6) outperforms HuBERT-continuous (LVE=9.49e-6) by ~15%, demonstrating that discretization provides a beneficial information bottleneck. The HuBERT representation without quantization performs comparably to (slightly worse than) Condition A (WavLM continuous, LVE=9.00e-6), indicating the performance advantage of Condition B comes from the discretization step, not from the underlying HuBERT encoder."
